    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the charge cannot stand. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold. Limb (b) requires the GPS trace to place the driver inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup at or before the 'arrived' event. It does not: the driver's own trace carries 37 fixes, all stationary (speeds 0.0 km/h), at a mean, minimum and maximum distance of 559.37 m from the pin, with derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count of 0. Limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of 300 seconds for a STANDARD zone; derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec is 0.0 seconds, so the waiting clock never started. The conjunctive test collapses and the fee is not chargeable. POL-NS-02 then gives the rider a full refund, and POL-NS-03 (wrong-entrance) cannot engage because the driver's closest approach, 559.37 m, is beyond that clause's 400 m ceiling — so no venue comparison and no pin-ambiguity goodwill payment arises.\n\nPOL-NS-05 applies on its own terms. At the 07:25:20 'arrived' marker the trace places the driver 559.37 m from the pin, far past the 300 m threshold, so the arrival marker is FALSE and does not start the waiting clock. No qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) governs squarely: full refund of the cancellation fee, no compensation, and the trip recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver. That is the referral above. (POL-NS-06 would reach the same refund as a 300-second dwell shortfall; the arithmetic is not in dispute.)\n\nOn the driver's escalation argument. You contend the arrival tap, the platform's 'Your driver has arrived' notice at 07:25:21 and your 'I have marked arrival.' message at 07:25:40 conflict with the trace, so POL-NS-09(b) should send this to a human reviewer. POL-NS-09(b) requires that no clause resolves the conflict. POL-NS-05 is the clause that resolves it: a marker set while the driver is more than 300 m from the pin is a false marker. The system notice and your own message do not supply an independent position fix — they restate the marker the trace contradicts — so they neither create an unresolved contradiction nor support arrival. The specific, datable position evidence wins.\n\nOn the rider's side. POL-NS-04 does not assist you: the chat log contains no rider message at all (only the system notice and the driver's message), and your own rider track shows no qualifying fix within the 100 m rider-presence radius. You do not need it — the refund follows from the driver's trace alone, and POL-NS-05(ii)/POL-NS-06 refund the fee whether or not the rider was present or responsive.\n\nCompensation. None is payable. POL-NS-07 funds a driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; it is not, and POL-NS-05(ii) states in terms that no compensation is payable where there is no qualifying in-geofence fix. The anti-farming question does not arise either way (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against 120 completed trips in 30 days, below both limbs), and no abuse-based escalation fires (rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0). The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09104-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) cannot help: POL-NS-06(i) needs a present, populated advisory to permit separate in-geofence intervals to be summed, and there are no such intervals here.\n\nConfidence. The deciding facts — driver position and absence of any qualifying in-geofence fix — are carried by the GPS trace and the trip record, both COMPLETE at weight 1.0, with 100% coverage, a 10-second cadence and no gaps, and the arrival marker coincides with a fix timestamp, so no impairment discount applies.",
